WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.417
These are the main habits from Module 11.

00:00:02.417 --> 00:00:05.267
Use CTEs to name logical stages.

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:10.462
Keep row grain explicit. Use windows when you need context without losing detail.

00:00:10.462 --> 00:00:13.682
Treat ORDER BY as part of the analytical definition.

00:00:13.682 --> 00:00:15.937
Write frame boundaries when they matter.

00:00:15.937 --> 00:00:19.352
And choose ranking functions based on the meaning of ties.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:24.022
Connect this idea to a hospital ranking visits and identifying readmissions.

00:00:24.022 --> 00:00:29.022
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:29.022 --> 00:00:36.372
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:36.372 --> 00:00:41.572
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:41.572 --> 00:00:46.880
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
